It pairs perfectly with the whimsical story told in Hexed , which follows a girl named Billie Doe &#8212; voiced by Steinfeld &#8212; as the discovery of her previously untapped magical abilities launches her &#8220;out of suburbia and into a spectacle-filled journey through a vast witch realm called Hexe,&#8221; according to a description. Rashida Jones, Jodie Foster, Walton Goggins, Tracey Ullman and Stephen Fry are also in the voice cast.

&#8220;Magic&#8221; reached No. 12 on the Billboard Hot 100 in 1984, but it&#8217;s far from The Cars&#8217; only hit. The Boston rock band also scored top 10 entries with &#8220;Drive&#8221; (No. 3), &#8220;Shake It Up&#8221; (No. 4), &#8220;You Might Think&#8221; (No. 7) and &#8220;Tonight She Comes&#8221; (No. 7).

Steinfeld has also earned her share of chart hits with five entries on the Hot 100 to date, led by 2016&#8217;s &#8220;Starving&#8221; with Grey and Zedd, which peaked at No. 12. She&#8217;s now becoming known for recording music in collaboration with the films she stars in, dropping &#8220;Dangerous&#8221; for Sinners in April of last year. “Blending music and acting like this feels like the fullest expression of who I am,” she told Billboard at the time.

